# REAL FIX 2026-08-31, direct instruction ("yes have the active desk be
# run from autostart"): the per-entity LAUNCH rows below (self/
# m8_redhorned/m1_ninjadragon/book-stack/asa/ava) are REMOVED - they were
# a static, hand-maintained list that silently drifted out of sync with
# the real active desk's own entity list (confirmed: it was missing a
# real placed tile, tile_rmmv_Inside_a2_1788175974, that the active
# desk's own .pdl genuinely declared). khtpm_taskbar_manager.c's own
# ktb_init() now calls livedesk_spawn_active_desk() on startup, which
# reads whatever session/desk is genuinely active and spawns its REAL,
# current entity list via the same proven livedesk_spawn_desk() logic a
# live desk switch already uses - a real, drift-free single source of
# truth. Keeping the static rows here TOO would race the manager's own
# startup spawn (confirmed live: tool-bar's own manager process starts
# and spawns the whole active desk before these later static LAUNCH rows
# even run, since livedesk_spawn_desk()'s own "already live" dedup check
# only skips a pal if it's ALREADDY registered - too early in that race
# to catch these), producing duplicate processes for some entities and,
# worse, silent double-launch failures dropping others entirely (self/
# m8_redhorned both observed missing after a reset with both mechanisms
# active). Only "tool-bar" stays - it's what starts the manager, whose
# own real startup path now owns spawning every desk entity, cursword
# included (see livedesk_ensure_cursword()'s own real dedup, unaffected
# by this change).
LAUNCH       | tool-bar              | '_.monads/_.livedesk-taskbar/ops/+x/khtpm_strip_parser.+x' '.'
